/// The agent-status channels, declared as a set. Their presence is what turns
/// the facility on: the host builds the `system:agent-status` participant iff
/// this document declares all three, and refuses to boot on some without the
/// rest.
///
/// The addresses are fixed rather than parameterized: a consumer, in tree or
/// out, has to know them without reading configuration. Nothing else about them
/// is brenn's: the deployment stamps them, sizes them, and grants other
/// principals access to them with ordinary ACLs.
///
/// `sessions` is a **state** channel: a snapshot of every conversation with a
/// running Claude Code process, each snapshot subsuming the one before it. It
/// is ephemeral because no process survives a restart, and a stale snapshot
/// after one is worse than none; an empty channel reads as "no sessions". On a
/// non-durable channel the retained window is the standing buffer, so
/// `retain_depth = 1` is what a consumer that starts later reads.
///
/// `ended` is a **fact** channel: one message per run of a session that ended,
/// which no later message subsumes. Durable, so a consumer down across a
/// restart still finds the facts in its window. Size `ended_retain` for the
/// longest consumer outage to survive, counted in session ends.
///
/// `accounts` is a **state** channel and durable: it is the account ledger's
/// storage, read back once at boot. `retain_depth = 1` is the state itself; a
/// `standing_retain_depth` of zero is refused at boot, since it would lose
/// every profile's spend at restart.
///
/// The reporter publishes every state change of every session, and a publish
/// the bus refuses ends the process, the send-rate gate's refusal included.
/// The channels state their own `send_rate`, so the host's
/// `default_send_rate` does not reach them. Boot refuses any of the three
/// below 240 in a burst and 30 a second sustained. A host whose sessions change
/// state faster than that declares the three channels itself, with a higher
/// rate.
///
/// TODO(agent-status-self-wake): A subscriber's own activity is in these
/// snapshots. An LLM agent that subscribes with a nonzero `push_depth` to
/// `sessions`, or to `accounts` while
/// it runs under an API-key profile, is woken by the snapshot its own last turn
/// caused, and so runs turns back to back with nobody asking, each one billed.
/// Such an agent reads them retained, with `push_depth = 0`.
assembly AgentStatus(ended_retain: Int = 64, accounts_standing: Int = 4) {
  channel sessions at "ephemeral:agent.sessions" {
    description = "Running Claude Code sessions (retained: the current set)";
    push_depth = 1;
    retain_depth = 1;
    send_rate = { burst = 240, refill_interval_secs = 1, refill = 30 };
  }
  channel ended at "brenn:agent.ended" {
    description = "Claude Code session runs that ended";
    push_depth = ended_retain;
    retain_depth = ended_retain;
    standing_retain_depth = ended_retain;
    send_rate = { burst = 240, refill_interval_secs = 1, refill = 30 };
  }
  channel accounts at "brenn:agent.accounts" {
    description = "Claude accounts: spend and refusal flags (retained: the ledger)";
    push_depth = 1;
    retain_depth = 1;
    standing_retain_depth = accounts_standing;
    send_rate = { burst = 240, refill_interval_secs = 1, refill = 30 };
  }
}
